## ${run:text}

The axis on every panel is **minutes since this run's own t0** (`meta.json` `windows.full[0]`, i.e. the start of measured load). The axis is 80 minutes wide — sized for the longest archived run — but every panel stops at **this** run's end, so a shorter run simply leaves the right side empty rather than continuing into whichever run came next.

The time picker is pinned to a fixed anchor and must stay there: the run is reached by the offset carried in the **Run** variable, not by the time range.
